    "title": "2025: A Year in Faith and Religion Reporting",
    "text": "• The article discusses major events and trends in faith and religion during 2025.\n• Pope Francis died in April 2025.\n• Cardinal Robert Francis Prevost was elected as Pope Leo XIV on May 8, 2025.\n• Pope Leo XIV is the 267th pope and the first from the United States.\n• Dallin H. Oaks became the new president of The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints on September 27, 2025, following the death of President Russell M. Nelson.\n• A shooting and fire occurred at a meetinghouse of The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints in Grand Blanc Township, Michigan, on September 28, 2025, resulting in four deaths and at least eight injuries.\n• Zohran Mamdani was elected as the first Muslim mayor of New York City in November 2025.\n• Erika Kirk, widow of Charlie Kirk, forgave her husband's killer.\n• A mass shooting occurred at a Hanukkah celebration in Bondi Beach, Sydney, Australia, resulting in 15 deaths and dozens of injuries.\n• Research from the Pew Research Center indicates that overall measures of religiosity have remained stable since 2020, and the rise of the 'nones' has leveled off.\n• Christian communities in Nigeria continue to face violence, with kidnappings reported.\n• Faith leaders are addressing the risks of AI encroaching on the sacred.\n• The Supreme Court issued rulings strengthening religious freedoms in 2025.\n• The article also mentions several other faith-related stories that were popular with readers.",
